# Embedded fonts for static renders

::summary
Static `file://` renders never painted Surf Display: `surfdoc.css` ships no
`@font-face` for it, and the `surf-display` font preset intentionally only
supplies a family stack (consumers self-host the files). 0.13.3 adds an
opt-in page option — `PageConfig::embed_fonts` — that embeds the face as a
data-URI `@font-face` plus the Inter `@import`. Default is **off** to
protect page weight; off is byte-identical to pre-0.13.3 output.
::

## The problem

The `surf-display` entry in the font preset table (`src/resolve.rs`) sets
only the family stack — `'Surf Display', -apple-system, …` — with no import
URL, because hosted surfaces (surf.space, the web shell) declare the
`@font-face` themselves in the host page. That is correct for hosted pages
and wrong for static output: an HTML file opened from disk has no host to
serve the woff2, so the stack silently falls back to system sans and the
brand display face never appears.

## The decision

- **Mechanism**: a boolean `embed_fonts` on `PageConfig`, honored by both
  `to_html_page` and `to_shell_page` (it lives in the shared head builder).
  When set, the head gains one `<style>` block containing the Inter
  Google-Fonts `@import` and a single `@font-face` for Surf Display
  (weight 900, `font-display: swap`) whose `src` is a base64 woff2 data
  URI. It is emitted *before* the inlined SurfDoc stylesheet so the face
  exists by the time the CSS font stacks resolve.
- **Default off**: the woff2 is 28.5 KB (38 KB as base64) added to every
  page. Documents that are served rather than opened from disk should keep
  using the host-declared face. Off emits nothing — existing pages are
  byte-for-byte unchanged, pinned by test.
- **Asset**: Surf Display Black is CloudSurf's own brand asset. It is
  vendored under `assets/fonts/` twice: `SurfDisplay-Black.woff2` (the
  binary, provenance copy) and `SurfDisplay-Black.woff2.b64` (its base64
  twin, consumed at compile time via `include_str!` so the crate needs no
  base64 dependency or build script). If the face is ever re-exported,
  regenerate both files together.
- **CLI surface**: the strategy/preview trees render through the `surf` CLI
  (`SURF_BIN`), so a user-facing `--embed-fonts` flag belongs to the `surf`
  repo, which forwards to this page option. `surf-lint` has no render
  command and is unaffected.

## Contract (pinned by tests)

- `embed_fonts: false` (the default) leaves the head byte-identical to
  0.13.2 output — no `@font-face`, no Inter import.
- `embed_fonts: true` emits exactly one Surf Display `@font-face` with a
  non-truncated woff2 data URI, on both the page and shell-page paths.
